power: supply: bq27xxx: use the internal sensor when the TS pin is unpopulated

The OnePlus 8 Pro (instantnoodlep, hw_version 15) does not populate the
bq27541's TS thermistor input: battery temperature in the vendor setup
comes from the PM8150B batt_therm ADC instead. With the TEMPS
pack-configuration bit at its default (external thermistor),
Temperature() reads the floating pin and reports a stuck bogus value
(52.1 C while the whole board sits at 38-42 C); the charger policy then
refuses to charge as "too hot".

Add a "ti,ts-pin-unused" DT property: when set, Temperature() comes
from InternalTemperature() (0x28), which TI confirms works regardless
of the TEMPS bit. The same off-spec firmware that reports SOC and
Temperature() in unexpected units reports InternalTemperature() in
decidegrees Celsius as well, so no Kelvin conversion on this path.

Verified on device by direct i2c reads: INT_TEMP tracks the board
(37.0 -> 36.9 C) while Temperature() stays pinned at 521.

Precedent: the OnePlus 6/6T shipped either bq27411 or bq27541 depending
on the production run, and misbinding the compatible produced exactly
this class of garbage readings (sdm845-mainline issue #36).
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery.c
@@ -1712,6 +1712,22 @@
 {
 	int temp;
 
+	if (di->use_internal_temp) {
+		temp = bq27xxx_read(di, BQ27XXX_REG_INT_TEMP, false);
+		if (temp < 0) {
+			dev_err(di->dev, "error reading internal temperature\n");
+			return temp;
+		}
+
+		/*
+		 * The same off-spec firmware reports InternalTemperature()
+		 * in decidegrees Celsius as well (see the Temperature()
+		 * comment below); no Kelvin conversion here.
+		 */
+		val->intval = temp;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	temp = bq27xxx_read(di, BQ27XXX_REG_TEMP, false);
 	if (temp < 0) {
 		dev_err(di->dev, "error reading temperature\n");
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_i2c.c
@@ -181,6 +181,17 @@
 
 	di->dev = &client->dev;
 	di->chip = id->driver_data;
+
+	/*
+	 * OnePlus 8 Pro (hw_version 15): the board does not populate the
+	 * bq27541 TS thermistor input (battery temperature comes from the
+	 * PMIC batt_therm in the vendor setup). With the default TEMPS
+	 * pack-configuration bit, Temperature() reads the floating pin and
+	 * reports a stuck bogus value. Boards that set ti,ts-pin-unused in
+	 * DT switch Temperature() to the internal sensor instead.
+	 */
+	di->use_internal_temp = device_property_read_bool(&client->dev,
+						 "ti,ts-pin-unused");
 	di->name = name;
 
 	di->bus.read = bq27xxx_battery_i2c_read;
--- a/include/linux/power/bq27xxx_battery.h
+++ b/include/linux/power/bq27xxx_battery.h
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@
 	int voltage_min_design;
 	int voltage_max_design;
 	bool removed;
+	/* DT ti,ts-pin-unused: Temperature() comes from the internal sensor */
+	bool use_internal_temp;
 	unsigned long last_update;
 	union power_supply_propval last_status;
 	struct delayed_work work;
